From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:48:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] engine: render immediately after feeding output, and survive
 detach

Three fixes to the same failure - a ghostty pane that stops repainting:

1. Force a *render*, not a draw. ghostty_surface_draw only re-presents
   already-built cells, so forcing it after new output redrew stale
   content and the pane still froze. ghostty_surface_render_now rebuilds
   from terminal state first. Verified in the configuration that was
   failing: an unfocused ghostty pane beside a focused cascadia pane now
   renders a full 4796-entry listing.

2. Detach no longer revokes the connection subscriptions. Tearing a tab
   into its own window detaches the content and re-attaches it, so
   revoking there severed the pty for the rest of the session. Cascadia
   does not touch its connection in Detach either.

3. AttachToNewControl re-captures the dispatcher. A torn-off tab lands on
   a *different* UI thread, and every marshalled event - title,
   scrollbar, swap chain - was being enqueued to the old window's
   dispatcher. Cascadia does the same via _setupDispatcherAndCallbacks;
   its Detach comment says why: "on a possibly new UI thread". It also
   re-raises SwapChainChanged so the new control can bind the handle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ee27Fih3vSPYsqrUBpUoc
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp    | 38 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index befe27c1e..beb100d56 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -214,14 +214,33 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // separate "begin painting" gate to open.
     }
 
+    // Detach happens when the content outlives its control - tearing a tab out
+    // into its own window is the everyday case. The core keeps running the
+    // whole time.
+    //
+    // The connection subscriptions therefore stay: revoking them here silently
+    // severed the pty for the rest of the session, so a torn-off tab never
+    // showed another byte. Cascadia does not touch its connection here either.
+    //
+    // What must go is anything bound to the UI thread we are leaving. The new
+    // control may live on a *different* UI thread, and events marshalled to the
+    // old dispatcher would never arrive.
     void GhosttyControlCore::Detach()
     {
-        _connectionOutputRevoker.revoke();
-        _connectionStateRevoker.revoke();
+        _dispatcher = nullptr;
     }
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::AttachToNewControl()
     {
+        // Re-capture the dispatcher on whichever UI thread we have landed on.
+        // Cascadia does the same via _setupDispatcherAndCallbacks, and its
+        // comment on Detach says why: "on a possibly new UI thread".
+        _dispatcher = winrt::Windows::System::DispatcherQueue::GetForCurrentThread();
+
+        // The new control binds the swap chain from this event's args, so a
+        // torn-off pane needs the current handle pushed at it.
+        _raiseSwapChainChanged();
+
         Attached.raise(*this, nullptr);
     }
 
@@ -324,12 +343,15 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // Measured: 80 notifies produced fewer than 20 wakes, and drawFrame
         // stopped being called entirely while the parser kept running.
         //
-        // ghostty_surface_draw is drawFrame(sync = true), which skips the
-        // needs_redraw gate and is documented as safe to call from another
-        // thread. It is what hwnd-host does on WM_PAINT - which is why the
-        // harness never showed this and a XAML pane, having no paint pump,
-        // always did.
-        ghostty_surface_draw(_surface);
+        // It must be render_now rather than draw: ghostty_surface_draw only
+        // re-presents the cells the render thread last built, so forcing it
+        // after new output just redraws stale content - measured, the pane
+        // still froze. render_now rebuilds from terminal state first.
+        //
+        // A pane in a XAML SwapChainPanel has no paint loop, so nothing else
+        // ever forces this. hwnd-host does it on WM_PAINT, which is why three
+        // phases of harness work never surfaced the problem.
+        ghostty_surface_render_now(_surface);
     }
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::_connectionStateChangedHandler()
